# MM Dual-Agent Rules (mm_vc_agent & mm_gh_agent)

## State Controls
- `MM_ON`/`MM_ENABLE`: activate agent pair workflow.
- `MM_OFF`/`MM_DISABLE`: pause workflow, standard chat.

## Plan Alignment & Execution (3-Phase Lifecycle)

### Phase 1 — Pre-Execution Alignment (Read-Only)
On `MM_BUG`/`MM_FEAT`: `mm_vc_agent` analyzes screenshots/logs, outputs Root Cause/Spec, Target Files, Blueprint.
**STOP:** no branches, commits, issues, PRs, or file edits. End turn; await developer alignment or `PROCEED`.

### Phase 2 — Execution & PR (on `PROCEED`)
`mm_gh_agent` creates GitHub Issue with blueprint, checks out branch. `mm_vc_agent` applies code changes, runs local validation. `mm_gh_agent` commits, pushes, opens PR (`Closes #<id>`). Yields for Live Local QA.

### Phase 3 — QA Sign-off & Sync (on `MM_BUGFIXED #<id>` / `MM_FEATDONE #<id>`)
`mm_gh_agent` verifies build, squash-merges PR, closes Issue, switches to `main`, pulls latest.

## Release Lifecycle (`MM_RELEASE` / `MM_RELEASEDONE`)
- `MM_RELEASE <version>`: checks clean tree, blocks if PRs open, warns on open issues, verifies SemVer, prevents tag collisions, checks out `release/v<version>`, bumps versions, commits, opens release PR in code freeze.
- `MM_RELEASEDONE`: squash-merges release PR (**do not delete branch**), tags version on `main`, publishes GitHub Release with auto-generated notes.

Confirm at critical transitions unless `--nocautious`.
